    "description": "Art Glass Cullet Chunk\nCobalt Blue with Rainbow Iridescent Finish\nDecorative Glass Specimen, 1.365 Pounds\nSubstantial decorative chunk of cobalt blue cullet slag glass displaying a vibrant iridescent carnival-style flash across fractured planes and smooth surfaces. Raw glass chunks like this were produced during the glassmaking process at heritage American glassworks, where excess furnace glass cooled into monolithic blocks before being fractured into decorative specimens prized for garden displays, lapidary projects, and paperweights.\nIntense translucent cobalt blue glass body with rich color depth\nExterior exhibits strong rainbow iridescence in vivid hues of gold, magenta, and turquoise\nNatural conchoidal fracturing showcasing glass cleavage, smooth waves, and raw crystalline textures\nMeasures approximately 4 inches by 2.25 inches by 3.25 inches; weighs 1.365 pounds\nCondition:\nFormed as a raw fractured glass chunk with natural sharp edges, conchoidal ridges, and cleavage faces inherent to slag glass. Clean surfaces with brilliant luster and no post-manufacture cloudiness or chemical damage.",
